#20237
Ground Floor of Bridge-tower.~
The ground floor of this tower is at least 30' X 30' with a 20' tall
ceiling.  The entire north wall is actually a large drawbridge that can
be dropped for horses, wagons and the like.  The south entrance contains
a giant portcullis, which is currently raised.  There is a ramp along the
east wall that leads up to the second storey of the tower.
~
